  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-7z-15 & =0 \\\\ 5x+2y-7z & =15 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ 5(5+4t)+2(3-3t)-7(-7+2t) & =15 \\\\ 25+20t+6-6t+49-14t & =15 \\\\ 80 & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect.",
